            <ArticleTitle>Dermatitis Cruris Pustulosa et Atrophicans.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116-117</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fifteen male soldiers having dermatitis cruris pustulosa et atrophicans were studied clinically, bacteriologically, histopathologicafly and immunologically. Average age at detection was 26 years. Skin lesions were classically distributed on the legs. Staphylococcus aure was grown from the lesions. Histopathological findings were of eczematous pattern with polymorphic cellular infiltrate in the dermis. IgG and IgA levels in blood were increased.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
